Opt-in line search for NLGEOM runs (SPAX robustness aid).

ccx already carries a secant line search along the Newton correction, but
gates it on static penalty contact (`mortar == 1` and contact elements
present).  This patch opens the same path to any NLGEOM run through
CCX_LINESEARCH=1: the residual-before (`resold`) is stored under the same
condition, the line-search block runs, and the factor is bracketed to
[0.05, 1.0] instead of the contact-tuned *CONTROLS defaults (whose ctrl
indexing is not worth trusting from C).

STATUS.  It works: the factor is computed and applied (observed 0.05-1.0
on the MMS cell, ~1.0 on the uniaxial path).  It is NOT required for the
20-50 % stretch validation -- the exact tangent reaches that on the
uniaxial problem with the line search off and on identically -- and it is
not sufficient by itself for the multi-axial MMS boundary field, whose
31 % corner displacements tangle the mesh at ~1-2 % strain regardless of
the step damping.  It is kept as an opt-in aid for paths that need a
bounded trial step, and as the hook for a future arc-length control.

  nonlingeo.c   the two gates, the clamp override, and the comment

--- nonlingeo.c
+++ nonlingeo.c
@@ -325,6 +325,15 @@
   i0ref=ctrl[0];irref=ctrl[1];icref=ctrl[3];
 
   sminls=ctrl[28];smaxls=ctrl[29];
+
+  /* SPAX: the generic F-bar line search uses a safe bracket; the
+     *CONTROLS defaults are contact-tuned and the ctrl indexing is not
+     worth trusting here */
+
+  if(getenv("CCX_LINESEARCH")!=NULL){
+    sminls=0.05;
+    smaxls=1.0;
+  }
   
